Last night I had an hair-raising adventure in Minetown, and part of it
involved how the game seemed to not handle sanctuary thematically.  I
wonder whether this is a case of Nethack Is Not Real Life, whether
this behavior is intended, or whether it might be a "feature."

My tourist was stuck in the Grotto town temple, which was thankfully
co-aligned.  I don't have telepathy yet, had been blinded by a raven,
had blundered into a shrieker, and soon I was surrounded by things the
shrieker presumably summoned (I swear there weren't that many monsters
in the area before I was blinded!).  With jumping boots and my camera
I manage to make it to the temple where I'm safe.  The problem is, I
have very few escape items: no pick-axe (left outside a store), a
sleep wand, no way to engrave Elbereth (not even a hard gem) and my
weapons are lots of darts at Expert and a silver dagger at Basic.
Worse, there is a dwarf outside clearing the walls, so whenever I step
into the doorway I'm attacked by three monsters.  Well with judicious
use of darts, camera and jumping I manage to kill an Uruk-hai and take
his long sword (which I advance to Basic) and then finally kill the
dwarf and grab his pick-axe.  I try to dig out the side of the temple
towards the stairs, but the dwarf or rock moles have beaten me to it
and I get attacked on all three sides there, too.  I try to dig east
to the downstairs, but same thing there, too.  I'm running out of
options that I can think of.

So finally I think to dig down through the temple floor to escape.
The problem is, with the front doorway (I'd kicked down the door so I
could jump diagonally to the dwarf's death square and back to grab the
pickaxe) and the two tunnels I'd dug, I kept seeing monsters and
stopping my digging.  Once I thought to blind myself with a towel
(remember that I didn't have telepathy yet), then the game allowed me
to dig my hole.  This is what I feel was handled poorly: even though I
could see the monsters I knew that it was impossible for them to
interrupt my digging because of the sanctuary, but the game did not
know that.  I'm guessing that if I'd had telepathy, I'd have been out
of luck (unless a watchman had blundered by a doorway, then I could
have zapped him to sleep and murdered him).

So anyway I did make it down one level (fortunately this was DL 7
since I don't have MR yet), found the upstairs, and with jumping
managed to make it barely back to the Minetown upstairs to escape.
That was a very exciting couple of hours and I am extremely pleased at
what nethack is able to accomplish with just a few ASCII characters!


